# mem as a program (roadmap os-server.md P12): its code and data segments,
# where the root put them (KCALL_SEGMENT), with the limits the CPU gives
# (LSL); its stack, at the data segment's bottom through the same selector;
# its break. (Where they are, and their limits, change with the build: only
# the selectors are checked.)
program: sh
install: C /BIN/MEM z-mem.rx
keys: mem\n
match: contains
---
/mnt/rx286$ mem
code:  selector 0007h, base {...}h, limit {...}h
data:  selector 000Fh, base {...}h, limit {...}h
stack: selector 000Fh, base {...}h, limit {...}h
break: {...}h
Nothing else is reachable: the kernel's selectors fault here.
/mnt/rx286$
